#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This dataset assembles the Container Trailer for use with a single 40' shipping container.
#
#Offsets at the Shape File Link level (the children to this dataset) will be needed to position the parts correctly.
#
#The front part should have no horizontal offsets.
#
#The mid part should be offset such that the pins line up properly with any container recievers, and such that the wheels are mounted to the axle rails at the rear of the segment.  For a single 40' container, only the pins on the front and rear segments interact with the container, so the offsets for the 2 x 20-ft container arrangement can be re-used.
#
#The rear part should be offset by the distance from the front of the container to the sprung mass coordinate system origin (675 mm) minus the total length of the container (12190 mm).
#
#The offset for the brake lights should match that of the rear section, and the reference lengths for the brake lights should match those of this assembly.
#
#Example:
#Offset for Front: 0 m
#
#Offset for Mid: 0.675 m - 6.05 m = -5.375 m
#
#Offset for Rear: 0.675 m - 12.19 m = -11.515 m
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

